{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0eb128f3673858b61ac29b3ec092b37a95ce3fb8ae2d00f54822e11cd41a6aef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent manages background tasks with configurable wait timeout and a concurrency cap (default 32, up to 64), and bash commands detach after a default 2-minute timeout with a SIGTERM-to-SIGKILL grace period."},{"claim_ids":["clm_30bcf644ee94d3af4f80a09281ab902a760de0c5d924057511c412a6f0240cb9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In the REPL, slash commands such as `/provider`, `/model`, `/effort`, `/preset`, `/config`, and `/preset-save` select providers and settings; Ctrl-T opens a transcript view in $PAGER and Ctrl-O shows the conversation as displayed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_362da9659487f20a7268af2e770bc0e5fa0d6edf7fced28afd16b535c1ef1db2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The bash tool runs commands through a configurable shell with a default 2-minute timeout before detaching; the maximum timeout a model may request defaults to 30 minutes, and no per-command permission prompts exist by design."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5b48e394d74fd4fa22e8c34b1d56a86245e86f2f59566d205b05e13fb73bab0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Presets can act as roles with description, system-prompt additions, and a tint; only presets with a description are advertised to the model as subagent delegation targets."},{"claim_ids":["clm_643e2a0ab2ba1350b992425809e4d12e3230d8b478ae6c689b84a7e507d5b08c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A wire-protocol trace can be collected via HAX_TRACE, capturing HTTP requests, statuses, and SSE events with credentials redacted; HAX_TRANSCRIPT mirrors the model-facing transcript to a file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b6385776d48222ef924641d5e9da65f1842e55b08ac8557f774829c385966c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Provider support includes OpenAI and compatible endpoints, Anthropic and compatible endpoints, Codex via ChatGPT login, OpenRouter, OpenCode Zen/Go, llama.cpp, ollama, and custom endpoints configured through providers.<id> blocks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9b59f4f15688487fb745cb0a2d3d2ba62e878be4b35204e34833b791474440f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Automatic compaction summarizes history near the context limit, triggered by a configurable percentage threshold (default 85), with the context limit overridable per model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bc9b23f179cc2547507574b6a9ac45cc57bb72cbc7b4a1e7c28673849daa812f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Settings resolve in order: current-process override, resumed conversation, environment, state.json, config.json, then default; the resumed tier covers provider, model, effort, and preset."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c9d5a1b88cdac4f985913f789a56f9a7e6ca46b6f036521f66d9ef710fe1bc11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"hax follows the XDG Base Directory specification: config at ~/.config/hax/config.json, remembered interactive selections and sessions under ~/.local/state/hax/, and a model-metadata cache at ~/.cache/hax/catalog.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f236947bb815e2739c3fd0f79ebf9a5e98f648719e749328734746913f61a046"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Model metadata (context limits, image capability, estimated spend) is fetched from models.dev and cached, refreshed in the background only when a catalog-identified provider needs it and the cache is stale; fetching can be disabled via catalog.url or catalog.refresh."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0eb128f3673858b61ac29b3ec092b37a95ce3fb8ae2d00f54822e11cd41a6aef","clm_30bcf644ee94d3af4f80a09281ab902a760de0c5d924057511c412a6f0240cb9","clm_362da9659487f20a7268af2e770bc0e5fa0d6edf7fced28afd16b535c1ef1db2","clm_5b48e394d74fd4fa22e8c34b1d56a86245e86f2f59566d205b05e13fb73bab0d","clm_643e2a0ab2ba1350b992425809e4d12e3230d8b478ae6c689b84a7e507d5b08c","clm_6b6385776d48222ef924641d5e9da65f1842e55b08ac8557f774829c385966c9","clm_9b59f4f15688487fb745cb0a2d3d2ba62e878be4b35204e34833b791474440f9","clm_bc9b23f179cc2547507574b6a9ac45cc57bb72cbc7b4a1e7c28673849daa812f","clm_c9d5a1b88cdac4f985913f789a56f9a7e6ca46b6f036521f66d9ef710fe1bc11","clm_f236947bb815e2739c3fd0f79ebf9a5e98f648719e749328734746913f61a046"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","id":"pg_2157ec69dedf5894bd3c01b9508dfc04","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/oleksandrchekhovskyi-hax-docs-configuration-md-7db349773eb7-01b9508dfc04.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"title":"OleksandrChekhovskyi/hax/docs/configuration.md @ 7db349773eb7","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0f36525f32f17b453ee4879d1d93804220d1cbd4626418aa397337225ec83e72"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI supports an interactive REPL, one-shot `-p` prompts (including stdin input), `-c` to continue the latest session, and `--resume`/`--resume=ID` session selection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_30bcf644ee94d3af4f80a09281ab902a760de0c5d924057511c412a6f0240cb9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In the REPL, slash commands such as `/provider`, `/model`, `/effort`, `/preset`, `/config`, and `/preset-save` select providers and settings; Ctrl-T opens a transcript view in $PAGER and Ctrl-O shows the conversation as displayed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_362da9659487f20a7268af2e770bc0e5fa0d6edf7fced28afd16b535c1ef1db2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The bash tool runs commands through a configurable shell with a default 2-minute timeout before detaching; the maximum timeout a model may request defaults to 30 minutes, and no per-command permission prompts exist by design."},{"claim_ids":["clm_63e789213d56068885577357f057d841d23bb86aa233dcce102425a6838d7f49"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs on Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, and OpenBSD; on Windows it is used under WSL, and the BSDs are build-from-source only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b6385776d48222ef924641d5e9da65f1842e55b08ac8557f774829c385966c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Provider support includes OpenAI and compatible endpoints, Anthropic and compatible endpoints, Codex via ChatGPT login, OpenRouter, OpenCode Zen/Go, llama.cpp, ollama, and custom endpoints configured through providers.<id> blocks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87b02669371e24fa28b69b6621de571692886c9c379d2e014c867058acb9e174"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building from source requires a C compiler, libcurl, jansson, meson, ninja, and pkg-config; fzf is additionally used for @file completion when available."},{"claim_ids":["clm_97e1694f9ea8308f67ad197642023ca9026e25398050262352d0d71c1840b615"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"hax is described as a minimalist, terminal-native coding agent implemented as a single native C binary with a small dependency set and low memory use."},{"claim_ids":["clm_defc6b4ab2f30fe75377dab8c4d6c2a1adfd56a0545a2f1f11d41873e00aa16f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project deliberately omits MCP marketplaces, a plugin runtime, IDE panels, and per-command permission prompts, composing instead via subprocesses and documenting each omission in docs/philosophy.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e89eb6ec1c02f1fa6269c0cd31c8271d35076382d550e55de55c8ba5876ede2a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By design hax lacks MCP marketplaces, a plugin runtime, IDE panels, and per-command permission prompts; the philosophy doc explains each omission and the pattern covering the need."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0f36525f32f17b453ee4879d1d93804220d1cbd4626418aa397337225ec83e72","clm_30bcf644ee94d3af4f80a09281ab902a760de0c5d924057511c412a6f0240cb9","clm_362da9659487f20a7268af2e770bc0e5fa0d6edf7fced28afd16b535c1ef1db2","clm_63e789213d56068885577357f057d841d23bb86aa233dcce102425a6838d7f49","clm_6b6385776d48222ef924641d5e9da65f1842e55b08ac8557f774829c385966c9","clm_87b02669371e24fa28b69b6621de571692886c9c379d2e014c867058acb9e174","clm_97e1694f9ea8308f67ad197642023ca9026e25398050262352d0d71c1840b615","clm_defc6b4ab2f30fe75377dab8c4d6c2a1adfd56a0545a2f1f11d41873e00aa16f","clm_e89eb6ec1c02f1fa6269c0cd31c8271d35076382d550e55de55c8ba5876ede2a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","id":"pg_297be6070c2a5995af29ac126f23ec58","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/oleksandrchekhovskyi-hax-readme-md-7db349773eb7-ac126f23ec58.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"title":"OleksandrChekhovskyi/hax/README.md @ 7db349773eb7","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028